\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Bondi's sign rules for two bodies released at rest, in the style of Forward's analysis~\cite  {forward1990}. Every body has positive inertial and passive mass; only the \emph  {active} (source) mass carries a sign---negative for the dashed bodies. (a)~Two positive-mass stars attract and fall together; (b)~two negative-mass stars repel and push apart; in both the forces oppose and the pair barycentre stays put. (c)~The mixed pair---the Bondi dipole: both forces point the \emph  {same} way, so the pair barycentre accelerates while the system carries zero total momentum in the signed bookkeeping. Each row is a run of the matrix in Table~\ref {tab:matrix}.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{1}{Bondi's sign rules for two bodies released at rest, in the style of Forward's analysis~\cite {forward1990}. Every body has positive inertial and passive mass; only the \emph {active} (source) mass carries a sign---negative for the dashed bodies. (a)~Two positive-mass stars attract and fall together; (b)~two negative-mass stars repel and push apart; in both the forces oppose and the pair barycentre stays put. (c)~The mixed pair---the Bondi dipole: both forces point the \emph {same} way, so the pair barycentre accelerates while the system carries zero total momentum in the signed bookkeeping. Each row is a run of the matrix in Table~\ref {tab:matrix}}{figure.1}{}}
