\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The four sign assignments under identical numerics: pair-barycentre drift at $d_0=8$. The mixed pair \texttt  {PM} runs away to $+6.41$ at $\Delta x=0.25$ and $+6.45$ at $\Delta x=0.5$, its space-reflected twin \texttt  {MP} to $-6.15$ at the same $\Delta x=0.5$ (a $4.7\%$ asymmetry), while \texttt  {PP} and \texttt  {MM} stay on the axis at $+0.036$ and $+0.012$---below one cell width of the finest grid, and shrinking under refinement (Fig.~\ref {fig:convergence}b).}}{6}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:controls}{{5}{6}{The four sign assignments under identical numerics: pair-barycentre drift at $d_0=8$. The mixed pair \texttt {PM} runs away to $+6.41$ at $\Delta x=0.25$ and $+6.45$ at $\Delta x=0.5$, its space-reflected twin \texttt {MP} to $-6.15$ at the same $\Delta x=0.5$ (a $4.7\%$ asymmetry), while \texttt {PP} and \texttt {MM} stay on the axis at $+0.036$ and $+0.012$---below one cell width of the finest grid, and shrinking under refinement (Fig.~\ref {fig:convergence}b)}{figure.5}{}}
